.pio

# Host test harness artifacts
sim/build/

# Third-party prebuilt image, downloaded not built
ESP32_GENERIC_S3-*.bin

# Secure boot signing key. Whoever holds this can sign firmware the device
# will accept, so it is the one file in this repository that must never be
# committed. Keep it offline; losing it means no future firmware updates,
# and leaking it means secure boot protects nothing.
secure_boot_signing_key.pem
*.pem

# Every other shape a key comes in. The Android release keystore is the live
# one: lose it and existing users cannot update, leak it and someone else can
# ship an update their phones will accept. It belongs outside this repository
# and in a GitHub Actions secret - see docs/RELEASE.md, "The Android release
# keystore". These patterns are the cheap half of that; preflight-secure.sh
# treats a key git is already tracking as compromised, which is the half that
# counts.
*.keystore
*.jks
*.p12

# Generated sdkconfig, one per PlatformIO environment.
#
# sdkconfig.defaults is the source of truth; these are built from it. Committing
# one makes it the truth instead, and it does NOT regenerate when the defaults
# change - so an edit to sdkconfig.defaults silently does nothing and the build
# reports success with none of the settings applied. That is how Wi-Fi stayed
# compiled in after being turned off (T17), and it is the same trap that
# produced four config faults in the secure environment.
sdkconfig.esp32s3
sdkconfig.esp32s3-*

# Agent worktrees. These are full checkouts of this repo on other branches;
# committing one would nest the repository inside itself.
.claude/worktrees/

# Internal notes: research that is not part of the published design.
# Ignored deliberately — see docs/internal/README if one exists.
docs/internal/

# Release artefacts, built by scripts/release.sh from a tag. Rebuildable by
# anyone from the tag, which is the point of T37, so committing them would only
# add a second copy that could disagree with the first.
release/

# MicroPython bring-up leftovers and a stray screenshot.
#
# main.py and ssd1306.py were how the very first board was made to draw
# anything, before there was firmware. They import `machine`, which does not
# exist in this project, and nothing references them. image.png was 1.4 MB of
# the largest file in the repository and is linked from nowhere.
#
# Kept out of the tree rather than deleted from disk: they are history, and
# git already has them if anyone wants to look.
main.py
ssd1306.py
image.png
ESP32_GENERIC_S3-*.bin

# Never commit these
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
dist/
*.keystore
*.jks
*.p12
keystore.properties
